testcase.failure:
Error: [vitest] No "NAV_ITEMS" export is defined on the "./NavBar" mock. Did you forget to return it from "vi.mock"?
If you need to partially mock a module, you can use "importOriginal" helper inside:

vi.mock(import("./NavBar"), async (importOriginal) => {
  const actual = await importOriginal()
  return {
    ...actual,
    // your mocked methods
  }
})

 ❯ src/surfaces/pageTitle.js:40:35
 ❯ src/components/Layout.jsx:20:1

Error: [vitest] No "NAV_ITEMS" export is defined on the "./NavBar" mock. Did you forget to return it from "vi.mock"?
If you need to partially mock a module, you can use "importOriginal" helper inside:

vi.mock(import("./NavBar"), async (importOriginal) => {
  const actual = await importOriginal()
  return {
    ...actual,
    // your mocked methods
  }
})

 ❯ src/surfaces/pageTitle.js:40:35
 ❯ src/components/Layout.jsx:20:1

